    "updated_at": "2022-10-20T13:09:49Z",
    "body": "You seem to try to run a nu script (generated by starship init nu) with a pwsh interpreter (iex). That will not work because they are different shells and interpreters, with different syntax. The error you see (`The term 'let-env' is not recognized as a name of a cmdlet, function, script file, or executable program.`) is exactly what you would expect; the nu syntax is not recognized by pwsh.\r\n\r\nI do not see how this would be a bug in Starship. This ticket should be closed as such, as invalid.\r\n\r\nIf you want to use starship with nushell in Windows Terminal, follow the readme as david said. As broader pointers; add a or open your nushell profile in Windows Terminal, and initialize starship by running the prepared nu script generated by starship init nu with the nu `source` command.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
